@startuml
title HydroModPy - Code-Level Component Diagram (Ports and Interfaces)
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

skinparam titleFontSize 14
skinparam legendFontSize 9
skinparam packageFontSize 10
skinparam componentFontSize 9
skinparam interfaceFontSize 9
skinparam noteFontSize 9

skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #64748B
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam interface {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7D6
  BorderColor #D4A72C
  FontColor #111827
}

skinparam component<<entry>> {
  BackgroundColor #FFE7B3
  BorderColor #B45309
  FontColor #7C2D12
}
skinparam component<<provider>> {
  BackgroundColor #E0F2FE
  BorderColor #0284C7
}
skinparam component<<consumer>> {
  BackgroundColor #EEF2FF
  BorderColor #6366F1
}
skinparam interface<<protocol>> {
  BackgroundColor #DCFCE7
  BorderColor #16A34A
}
skinparam interface<<abc>> {
  BackgroundColor #FCE7E7
  BorderColor #DC2626
}

legend right
|= Notation |= Meaning |
| <<entry>> | Public entry point |
| <<provider>> | Provides a contract |
| <<consumer>> | Requires a contract |
| <<protocol>> | Python Protocol |
| <<abc>> | Python ABC |
| -() | Provided port |
| -( | Required port |
| --> | Strong dependency |
| ..> | Weak dependency |
endlegend

package "Public API" {
  component "hydromodpy.__init__" as API <<entry>>
  component "hydromodpy.project.Project" as Project <<entry>>
  component "hydromodpy.project_runner.ProjectRunner" as ProjectRunner <<consumer>>
  component "hydromodpy.project_catalog.ProjectCatalog" as ProjectCatalog <<consumer>>
  component "hydromodpy.calibration_dispatch" as CalibrationDispatch <<entry>>
}

package "Workflow Runtime" {
  component "hydromodpy.workflow.orchestrator" as Orchestrator
  component "hydromodpy.workflow.runner.Pipeline" as Pipeline
  component "hydromodpy.workflow.launcher_protocol.Launcher" as LauncherProto <<protocol>>
  component "hydromodpy.simulation.execution.runner.SimulationRunner" as SimulationRunner <<provider>>
}

package "Calibration Runtime" {
  component "hydromodpy.calibration.runner.CalibrationRunner" as CalibrationRunner <<consumer>>
  component "hydromodpy.calibration.engine.CalibrationEngine" as CalibrationEngine <<provider>>
  component "hydromodpy.calibration.runners.trial.run_trial_light" as TrialRunner <<consumer>>
  component "hydromodpy.calibration.runners.trial.promote_prepared_trial" as TrialPromote <<consumer>>
  component "hydromodpy.calibration.optimizer.Optimizer" as CalibrationOptimizerProto <<protocol>>
  component "hydromodpy.calibration.adapters.*" as CalibrationAdapters <<provider>>
}

package "Storage and Catalog" {
  component "hydromodpy.results.catalog.protocol.SimulationStore" as SimulationStoreProto <<protocol>>
  component "hydromodpy.results.catalog.facade.SimulationCatalog" as SimulationCatalog <<provider>>
  component "hydromodpy.data.store.DataStore" as DataStore
  component "hydromodpy.data._base_manager_common.SourceConfigProtocol" as SourceConfigProto <<protocol>>
}

package "Solver and Display Contracts" {
  component "hydromodpy.core.contracts.solver_registry.SolverRegistryProvider" as SolverRegistryProto <<protocol>>
  component "hydromodpy.solver.base.protocol.SolverAdapter" as SolverAdapterProto <<protocol>>
  component "solver backends" as SolverBackends <<provider>>
  component "hydromodpy.display.figure.Figure" as FigureProto <<protocol>>
  component "hydromodpy.display.figure.BaseFigure" as BaseFigureABC <<abc>>
}

API --> Project : exposes public API
API --> CalibrationDispatch : exposes calibration API
Project --> ProjectRunner : run facade
Project --> ProjectCatalog : catalog facade

ProjectRunner --> Orchestrator : prepare / execute
ProjectRunner --> CalibrationDispatch : calibrate facade
Orchestrator --> Pipeline : canonical flow
Orchestrator -( LauncherProto : requires launcher
SimulationRunner -() LauncherProto : provides launcher

CalibrationDispatch --> CalibrationRunner : dispatch calibration
CalibrationRunner --> CalibrationEngine : drive ask/tell loop
CalibrationRunner --> TrialRunner : evaluate trials
CalibrationRunner --> TrialPromote : promote best runs
CalibrationEngine -( CalibrationOptimizerProto : requires optimizer
CalibrationAdapters -() CalibrationOptimizerProto : provides adapters
TrialRunner ..> LauncherProto : uses launcher
TrialPromote ..> LauncherProto : full rerun
TrialPromote ..> SimulationStoreProto : persist promoted runs

ProjectCatalog -( SimulationStoreProto : queries store
ProjectRunner -( SimulationStoreProto : stores / reads runs
SimulationCatalog -() SimulationStoreProto : provides simulation store

DataStore -( SourceConfigProto : consumes source config
DataStore ..> SimulationCatalog : uses catalog backend

Orchestrator -( SolverRegistryProto : resolves solvers
SolverBackends -() SolverAdapterProto : provides adapters
Orchestrator ..> SolverAdapterProto : dispatches via registry

BaseFigureABC -() FigureProto : provides figure contract

note bottom of Orchestrator
  Central workflow coordinator.
  The runtime path is shared by CLI, API and notebooks.
end note

note bottom of SimulationCatalog
  Workspace-level result store.
  Implements the read/write catalog contract.
end note

note bottom of SimulationRunner
  Default in-tree launcher.
  Conforms structurally to the Launcher protocol.
end note

note bottom of CalibrationRunner
  Coordinates the calibration workflow.
  Drives the ask/tell loop and optional promotion.
end note

note bottom of CalibrationEngine
  Ask/tell engine used by calibration adapters.
  Resolves suggestions and convergence.
end note

note right
  **DESIGN PATTERNS**

  1) Facade: public API and project accessors
  2) Orchestrator: workflow and calibration coordinators
  3) Pipeline: ordered execution path
  4) Registry: solver and optimizer lookup
  5) Adapter: solver and calibration backends
  6) Ports & Adapters: conceptual ports vs real Protocol/ABC
  7) Strategy: backend selection at runtime
end note

note right
  Code-level view: the diagram highlights the real Python contracts
  used at the boundaries between orchestration, solvers, data loading
  and result storage.

  Provided ports are shown with -(). Required ports are shown with -(.
  Concrete plugin implementations live outside the core modules.
end note

@enduml